flowchart TB
%% PREAMBLE PIPELINE. Split from pipeline.mmd. Starts at the task number.
%% Ends with an active task and an initialized worktree, or with an exit.
%% Rules that apply everywhere, not steps:
%%   1. Every git interaction goes through a script. Never prose.
%%   2. Every read and write of tasks.json is atomic.
%%   3. A script that fails operationally, as opposed to returning a verdict,
%%      exits the run as run-failed. No step is retried after it has mutated
%%      anything. How far the exit workflow can run depends on where the failure
%%      happened, and there are three cases in this phase:
%%        before the task is active - report and stop; there is no run to write to
%%        active, no worktree      - exit workflow runs; modified files records []
%%        active, with worktree    - exit workflow runs in full
%%   4. A mutating box whose result is lost is never blindly retried and never
%%      assumed failed. Each one has a read-only reconciliation check that reads
%%      the world and decides whether it already happened. A safe idempotent
%%      rerun happens only after reconciliation proves it did not complete. Only
%%      an ambiguous loss is run-failed.
%%   5. A task stays unavailable to another run from "mark the task active" until its
%%      archive lands. "is the task active?" and "mark the task active" are drawn as two
%%      boxes but are one atomic read-modify-write of tasks.json under rule 2: nothing can
%%      make the task active between the two.
%% Diamond definitions where the name alone is not enough:
%%   is the worktree safe to use?      - structural: it opens, it is on the task's
%%                                       branch, its submodules are intact
%%   is the previous run's work resumable?
%%                                     - did the previous implementor record where
%%                                       in the plan it stopped?
%% Exit types this pipeline can produce:
%%   invalid-number     - not in tasks.json or completedTasks.json
%%   not-open           - already completed
%%   already-active     - a previous run left the task active
%%   blocked            - an open blocker remains
%%   run-failed         - a script failed operationally
%% run-failed is deliberately not drawn as an edge. It can leave ANY green box,
%% so drawing it would add one edge per box and hide the flow. Rule 3 is its
%% specification: a non-zero exit from any script goes straight to the exit
%% workflow with exit type run-failed and the script's stderr as the note.
%% Every exit here goes to the exit workflow, which picks its own tail.
%% invalid-number, not-open and already-active are the only exits that write
%% nothing to tasks.json: the first two have no open task record to write to, and
%% the third must not touch a run that belongs to another invocation. The exit
%% workflow gives those three its report-only tail; blocked and run-failed get
%% the full tail. That choice is drawn there, not here.
%% The active task and initialized worktree this pipeline emits are the input to
%% the planning pipeline.

  TASKNUM["Input: { task number }"] --> QV
  QV{"is task number valid?"} -- "no<br/>exit type: invalid-number<br/>exit note: task number is in neither tasks.json nor completedTasks.json" --> EXITWF
  QV -- yes --> Q0{"is task open?"}
  Q0 -- "no<br/>exit type: not-open<br/>exit note: task is already completed" --> EXITWF
  Q0 -- yes --> QA{"is the task active?"}
  QA -- "yes<br/>exit type: already-active<br/>exit note: a previous run left the task active" --> EXITWF
  QA -- no --> MARK["mark the task active in tasks.json"]
  MARK --> QB{"is task blocked?"}
  QB -- "yes<br/>exit type: blocked<br/>exit note: an open blocker remains" --> EXITWF
  QB -- no --> Q1{"does a worktree exist?"}
  Q1 -- no --> NEW["create a worktree"]
  NEW --> GEN["auto generate docs"]
  GEN --> INIT
  Q1 -- yes --> QS{"is the worktree safe to use?"}
  QS -- no --> QRS{"is the previous run's work resumable?"}
  QRS -- no --> RESET["reset the worktree"]
  RESET --> GEN
  QRS -- yes --> UPD
  QS -- yes --> UPD["update auto generated docs"]
  UPD --> INIT["init submodules recursively"]
  INIT --> RECEIPT["Receipt: { active task, initialized worktree }"]

  EXITWF["exit workflow"] --> FAIL_RECEIPT["Receipt: { exitType, exitNote }" ]

  classDef script fill:#2f7d46,stroke:#1e5c31,color:#ffffff
  classDef prose fill:#e0b400,stroke:#a88600,color:#1a1a1a
  classDef output fill:#3b6ea5,stroke:#254a70,color:#ffffff
  classDef fail fill:red,stroke:#254a70,color:#ffffff
  class QV,Q0,QA,MARK,QB,Q1,NEW,GEN,QS,QRS,RESET,UPD,INIT script
  class EXITWF fail
  class TASKNUM,RECEIPT,FAIL_RECEIPT output
